    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Alternatively, if the star were small, the life-supporting planet would have to have a close orbit round it and also provide the perfect conditions for life forms to develop.",
      "translation": "或者，如果恒星很小，维持生命的行星必须有一个紧挨着它的运行轨道，并且还必须为生命形式的发展提供完美的条件。",
      "startTime": 87.92,
      "endTime": 101.36,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "alternatively",
            "pos": "adv.",
            "meaning": "或者，作为替代"
          },
          {
            "word": "orbit",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "轨道"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "But how would we find such a planet? At present, there is no telescope in existence that is capable of detecting the presence of life.",
      "translation": "但是我们如何找到这样的行星呢？目前，还没有一种现存的望远镜能够探测到生命的存在。",
      "startTime": 101.37,
      "endTime": 112.37,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "telescope",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "望远镜"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "The development of such a telescope will be one of the great astronomical projects of the 21st century.",
      "translation": "研制这种望远镜将是21世纪重大的天文项目之一。",
      "startTime": 112.38,
      "endTime": 121.14,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "astronomical",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "天文学的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "It is impossible to look for life on another planet using earth-based telescopes. Our own warm atmosphere and the heat generated by the telescope would make it impossible to detect objects as small as planets.",
      "translation": "使用地球上的望远镜是不可能在另一个行星上寻找生命的。我们自己温暖的大气层和望远镜产生的热量会使探测行星那么小的物体变得不可能。",
