    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Even a telescope in orbit round the earth, like the very successful Hubble telescope, would not be suitable because of the dust particles in our solar system.",
      "translation": "即使是像非常成功的哈勃望远镜那样绕地球轨道运行的望远镜也不适用，因为我们的太阳系中存在尘埃颗粒。",
      "startTime": 137.1,
      "endTime": 149.02,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "particle",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "微粒"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "A telescope would have to be as far away as the planet Jupiter to look for life in outer space, because the dust becomes thinner the further we travel towards the outer edges of our own solar system.",
      "translation": "望远镜必须远在木星那么远的地方才能到外层空间寻找生命，因为我们向太阳系外缘走得越远，尘埃就越稀薄。",
      "startTime": 149.03,
      "endTime": 163.96,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "Jupiter",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "木星"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Once we detected a planet, we would have to find a way of blotting out the light from its star, so that we would be able to 'see' the planet properly and analyse its atmosphere.",
      "translation": "一旦我们探测到一颗行星，我们就必须想办法遮住来自其恒星的光线，这样我们才能清楚地“看到”这颗行星并分析其大气层。",
      "startTime": 163.97,
      "endTime": 176.37,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "blot",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "遮盖"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "In the first instance, we would be looking for plant life, rather than 'little green men'. The life forms most likely to develop on a planet would be bacteria.",
      "translation": "首先，我们将寻找植物生命，而不是“小绿人”。行星上最有可能发展的生命形式将是细菌。",
      "startTime": 176.38,
      "endTime": 188.84,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
